## ⚡ Overview

Evaluating credit risk shouldn't be a black box. This project not only predicts whether a loan applicant is a **High Risk** or **Low Risk** candidate but also explains **WHY** using **SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations)**. 

<div align="center">
  <img src="https://cdn.dribbble.com/users/1355613/screenshots/15252730/media/28f348daf9ebb7dd9808f23ece29d91f.gif" alt="Project Demo" width="700" style="border-radius: 10px;">
</div>

---

## ✨ Standout Features

- 🎯 **High-Accuracy Predictions**: Powered by robust ML algorithms tailored for financial datasets.
- 🧠 **Explainable AI (XAI)**: Visualizes the impact of each feature (e.g., income, age, credit history) on the final decision using SHAP.
- 🎛️ **Optimized Thresholds**: Implements custom decision boundaries (`best_threshold.pkl`) to balance precision and recall.
- 🌐 **Interactive Web UI**: A sleek frontend to input applicant details and view real-time risk analysis.
- ☁️ **Cloud-Ready**: Pre-configured `render.yaml` for instant deployment.

---

## 🛠️ Architecture & Tech Stack

<details>
<summary><b>Click to expand the Tech Stack! 🚀</b></summary>

| Category | Technology |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Backend & API** | Python, FastAPI / Flask (`main.py`) |
| **Machine Learning** | Scikit-Learn, Pandas, NumPy, XGBoost |
| **Model Interpretability** | SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) |
| **Frontend UI** | HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JS (`static/`) |
| **Deployment** | Render (`render.yaml`, `runtime.txt`) |

</details>

